# The three loops over the index space compute from the index (and an
# offset) alone, so their bodies only compute and they are structured;
# vectorized, they run on the target's lanes, and each loop that computes
# 64-bit lanes is the 64-bit version beside one computing them in 32 bits,
# under a bound on n and the offset that the first run's input is below and
# the second's above, a negative offset above it either way: both versions
# must give the numbers of 64-bit lanes.
owned: structured-loops
lowered: vectorized narrowed-lanes
